{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794103993,"nonce":"kNmHPuz2K5SezEU10Uo3dUQYGYQ=","title":"Show and new: `e` writes the text in $EDITOR, and expand moves to `x`","message":"## Design\n\n**Aspects changed:** `doc/design/tui.md` (the letters table, \"Changing what is expanded\"), `doc/design/views.md` (\"The comment box\", \"Editing the description\", \"The creator page\"); `host/quickstart.md` (`esc e` → `esc x`).\n\n- `esc e` / `alt+e` opens the text in an external editor on: show's comment box (on it or in its text), show's description tab and its editor, and new's description box. Elsewhere it rings.\n- **Expand moves to `esc x` / `alt+x`**, so `e` is edit. `x` is free on the palette and `alt+x` is not a textarea key; `alt+e` is not one either, so `e` works from inside the text.\n- **Which editor:** git's order, `GIT_EDITOR`, `core.editor`, `VISUAL`, `EDITOR`, then `vi`, via `gitcli`'s `GetCoreEditor`: a tracker kept in git uses the editor git does.\n- **How:** the draft (or, for the description, the editor's draft or else the current body) is written to a temp `.md` file, and the screen is suspended while the editor runs (`tea.ExecProcess`).\n- **On exit** the text comes back into the box as the draft, the cursor in the text; `Enter` still sends or writes. The editor failing, or the file unchanged, leaves the draft as it was.\n- Not \"saving sends\": on new, `Enter` accepts the draft rather than creating, so one exit would mean two things.\n- The hints name `esc e` on the box and in its text (on the bottom line only, see the hints story).\n- **Deliberately absent: the command line.** `issue comment new` stays plumbing: an agent passes BODY or `-`, and an editor prompt would block it.\n\nDesign approved by Luis on 2026-11-07, in a combined review of four stories (box column, side-table arrows, $EDITOR, hints on the bottom line).","files":null,"fields":{"area":["tui"],"priority":"medium","status":"in-progress","type":"story"}}]}